<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<LightningComponentBundle xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
    <isExposed>true</isExposed>
    <!--
        DISPLAY LABELS. masterLabel and description are what an admin reads in the Lightning App
        Builder palette, so they track the card title, which has now carried five names: "Recent
        Packages" to "Recent Portfolios" to "Portfolio Deals" (retracted) to "Property Packages" and
        now back to "Portfolio Deals" - the plural of the underlying object's own label.

        Entry 3 was RETRACTED at the time because it collided with an Opportunity stage value named
        "Portfolio Deal" that was then live. That stage value, its path step and finally the three
        Opportunity fields behind it were retired in phases A1-A3 of the Portfolio Deal rename, so the
        collision no longer exists and the same wording is now correct rather than forbidden.

        THE BUNDLE'S API NAME IS `recentPortfolioDeals`, RENAMED FROM `recentPackages` IN PHASE B4 OF
        THAT SAME PROGRAM. The predecessor's note here read that the API name "stays `recentPackages`"
        and that re-pointing the API names was "the rename program's job, done wholesale in one
        authorised phase - not a passing edit's". This IS that phase (design
        agent-output/design-requirements-portfolio-deal-rename.md, section 5 phase B4 and section 6),
        so the bundle, its Apex (PortfolioDealController.getRecentPortfolioDeals), the object
        (Portfolio_Deal__c) and the labels all moved together. An LWC bundle rename is a delete and
        create and it DOES break any page that binds the old API name, so Lead_Funnel.flexipage-meta.xml
        was updated in the same wave; a page still naming `recentPackages` renders nothing.
    -->
    <masterLabel>Portfolio Deals</masterLabel>
    <description>Multi-property broker emails that arrived most recently, newest first, with each deal's broker and property count. Intended for the Acquisition app's Lead Funnel tab.</description>
    <targets>
        <target>lightning__AppPage</target>
        <target>lightning__HomePage</target>
    </targets>
</LightningComponentBundle>
